From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:54:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] L2 prefetch: a TileLang kernel family beside the CuTe one

VLLM_L2_PREFETCH_KERNELS=tilelang selects l2_prefetch_tilelang.py: the same work split (grid x 128 threads over the segment table, one bulk prefetch per 4 KB chunk rounded down to 16 bytes) and the same two PTX instructions (createpolicy.fractional.L2::evict_last and cp.async.bulk.prefetch.L2 with the cache hint), loops in TileLang and the PTX in a small header. CuTe stays the default until a serving A/B. On sm_121a it compiles to 22 registers with UBLKPF.L2 per chunk.
